#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:5
#: 6961390e43ed4cee8c356573e22fd539
msgid "STABILIZE Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:7
#: b22cf18ddda745fe99af273d0520041c
msgid "RC control with simple stabilization. If you let go of the sticks then Plane will level the plane. This is a bit like flying a plane with a lot of dihedral. You will find that while it is possible to do maneuvers like rolls and loops in stabilize mode, the tendency of the plane to right itself will make these maneuvers difficult. For people wanting the plane to mostly fly itself, with the pilot just telling it where to fly, you are better off using the :ref:`FLY BY WIRE_A (FBWA) <fbwa-mode>` mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:15
#: a277df9d9d79495fb884e84cc0fe540b
msgid "In stabilize mode the throttle is limited by the ``THR_MIN`` and ``THR_MAX`` settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/stabilize-mode.rst:20
#: 82cac37e981c4dccbba64424b2dddca2
msgid "STABILIZE mode is not a good mode to use for tuning the control loops. You are far better off using :ref:`FLY BY WIRE_A (FBWA) <fbwa-mode>` for that."
msgstr ""
